# MetaService settings. Copy this file to control-plane/arm64/.env and make it owner-only (mode 600). The Root refuses to start if anyone else can read it.
# Never commit the real file. A blank value means "not set". No MetaService tool ever prints a value from this file.
#
# WHAT IS REQUIRED?  Nothing. With every line empty, MetaService starts and works on this Mac only (the chat will say it has no AI yet).
#
# PRIMARY, what you will normally set, in this order:
#   1. AI_BASE_URL, AI_API_KEY, AI_DEFAULT_MODEL            so the chat can answer                     (all three, or none)
#   2. PUBLIC_BASE_URL, CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN/_ACCOUNT_ID/_ZONE_ID   to open the panel from outside the Mac   (all four, or none)
#
# OPTIONAL, only when you need them:
#   ROOT_SETUP_TOKEN, ROOT_AGENT_BIND, ROOT_AGENT_PORT, AI_MAX_TOKENS, AI_CAPABILITY_SECONDS, SCAN_SUBNET, ROUTER_URL, ROUTER_USER, ROUTER_PASSWORD

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRIMARY 1: AI for the chat. Set all three or none. The address is https, or http to a private address (a local model server).
# The key lives only here: machines and VMs never hold it. Use a model your provider answers for; the parent proxies every chat reply.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AI_BASE_URL=
AI_API_KEY=
AI_DEFAULT_MODEL=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRIMARY 2: reaching the panel from outside (all four lines, or none). PUBLIC_BASE_URL is the https address the panel is served at, with no port and
# no path, for example https://meta.example.com. Leave it empty for local use. Once set, the panel answers only under that name.
# The three CLOUDFLARE_ lines let `./install.sh remote up` make the tunnel, the route and the DNS record on a tunnel of its own (another project's
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_ID is never used and is refused here). The token needs Zone DNS: Edit and Account Cloudflare Tunnel: Edit. It is read only from this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PUBLIC_BASE_URL=
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL: the first-run lock. Creating the admin login needs this token (16 or more characters). Leave it empty and on the first start the Root makes
# one and writes it here for you. You only set it yourself if you want to choose it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ROOT_SETUP_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL: where Agents and chats reach the Root. The operator panel is always on 127.0.0.1 and has its own admin login (made on the first visit).
# Only needed to let Agents on OTHER machines enroll and send heartbeats: set the address to this Mac's LAN address (the port defaults to 9102).
# Leave both empty to manage only this Mac.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ROOT_AGENT_BIND=
ROOT_AGENT_PORT=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL: limits for the AI. Most tokens in one reply (1 to 4096, default 512) and how long a chat's pass lasts in seconds (60 to 3600, default 600).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
AI_MAX_TOKENS=
AI_CAPABILITY_SECONDS=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL: Find machines. With these empty the scan finds the private network this Mac is on by itself, sweeps it with nmap and reads the ARP table.
# SCAN_SUBNET: a private network no wider than /22, only if the automatic choice is wrong. ROUTER_*: a read-only MikroTik account, only if you have a
# MikroTik router (a TP-Link Omada router is not supported, leave these empty).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCAN_SUBNET=
ROUTER_URL=
ROUTER_USER=
ROUTER_PASSWORD=
